   "tag": "p",
   "text": "ARCHAEOLOGY CATALOGUE · ROW BA-076 temple ritual context; ending reconstruction disputed"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "What it supports. Demsky publishes the preserved trumpeting-place wording of a Hebrew inscription recovered in Mazar's Temple Mount excavations."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "What it does not. Its third word is broken. Demsky, Mazar, Yadin and Ben-Hayyim offer competing completions; none should be printed as surviving text. Association with Sabbath signaling combines the inscription with Josephus and ritual sources."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "Bears on: Second Temple worship background"
